{"name":"Jarrah","hex":"#827058","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jarrah","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A eucalypt tree of species Eucalyptus marginata, occurring in the southwest of Western Australia.","The wood of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jarrah"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eucalyptus marginata","blocks":[{"text":"Eucalyptus marginata, commonly known as jarrah, is a plant in the myrtle family, Myrtaceae and is endemic to the south-west of Western Australia. It is a tree with rough, fibrous bark, leaves with a distinct midvein, white flowers and relatively large, more or less spherical fruit. Its hard, dense timber is insect resistant although the tree is susceptible to dieback. The timber has been utilised for cabinet-making, flooring and railway sleepers. It is known as djarraly in Noongar language and historically as Swan River mahogany."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Jarrah_tree_burls_01_gnangarra.JPG/330px-Jarrah_tree_burls_01_gnangarra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eucalyptus_marginata","wikidata":"Q140557"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Jarrah_bark.jpg/120px-Jarrah_bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Jarrah_bark.jpg/250px-Jarrah_bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Jarrah_bark.jpg/120px-Jarrah_bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJarrah_bark.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/The_Looming_Relic.jpg/250px-The_Looming_Relic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte